<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasan ibn Ali</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 625–<a href="/years/670">670 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasan ibn Ali was a grandson of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prophet-muhammad">Prophet Muhammad</a> and the elder son of Ali, the fourth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>. After Ali's assassination in 661 he was briefly recognised as caliph in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a>. He then abdicated in favour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muawiya-i">Muawiya</a>, ending the Rashidun Caliphate and opening the way to Umayyad rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hasan-ibn-ali.jpg" alt="Hasan ibn Ali" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Effective Light · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AD%D8%B3%D9%86_%D8%A7%D8%A8%D9%86_%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%8A.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
